    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6692A\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to authorize the town of Seneca Falls to offer an optional twen-\nty-year retirement plan to a certain formerly employed police officer\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Town of Seneca Falls to offer an optional twenty-year\nretirement plan to a certain formerly employed police officer\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one allows Jamie Buffone, a police officer employed by the City\nof Ithaca, who had previously been employed as a police officer by the\nVillage now Town of Seneca Falls to participate in the optional twenty-\nyear retirement plan.\n\nSection two states that all costs associated with this legislation shall\nbe borne by the Town of Seneca Falls.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOfficer Jamie Buffone recently sought to retire from the City of Ithaca\nand was informed by the State and Local Police and Fire System that\nthrough no fault of her own, she had been placed in the 375-i plan when\nshe had been employed by the Village of Seneca Falls.\n\nOfficer Buffone was placed in the correct retirement plan during her\ntime serving the City of Ithaca. This legislation will enable Officer\nBuffone to have the time accrued while working for the Village of Seneca\nFalls attributed to the correct twenty-year retirement plan.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nIf this bill is enacted during the 2024 legislative session, there will\nbe an immediate past service cost of approximately $108,000 which will\nbe borne by the Town of Seneca Falls as a one-time payment. This esti-\nmate assumes that payment will be made on February 1, 2025. This bill\nwill not increase the future annual contributions of the City of Ithaca.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
